IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cp4-nouns`
IMPORT `cp4-calendar`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, sections 63, 63.1 and 64 -- THE SURVIVOR'S PENSION AND REMARRIAGE.
--
-- Section 63 once ended a survivor's pension on remarriage (subsection (2)), kept the right to a new pension
-- on the next spouse's death (subsection (3)) and revived the old one if the marriage ended otherwise than by
-- death (subsection (4)); it also allows only one survivor's pension at a time (subsection (6)) and withholds
-- the pension where the contributor died within a year of the marriage (subsections (7) and (7.1)). Section
-- 63.1 stops remarriage ending the pension, for a remarriage after "the coming into force of this section",
-- and lets earlier cases apply to have a pension commenced or reinstated. Subsections 63(8) to (10) confine
-- subsections (3) to (5) to the cases that were pending when section 63.1 came into force.
--
-- THE DATE OF COMING INTO FORCE. The text of section 63.1 says "the coming into force of this section" and
-- gives no date, and the text read does not say elsewhere. It is therefore a stated input,
-- `the day section 63.1 comes into force`, wherever a rule needs it (NOTES.md, "Cross-references out of my
-- ranges" and the fork register). Section 64 is repealed.
--
-- Out of range, taken as plain inputs: that the person is a survivor (s 42(1)), the amount of a survivor's
-- pension (s 58, in this piece), the prescribed person who may apply on behalf of another (regs, piece cr2).

§ `Section 63 -- remarriage and the survivor's pension`

§§ `Section 63.1(1) -- remarriage after section 63.1 comes into force`

-- src:2100 | Subsections do not apply
-- src:2101 | 63.1 (1) Subsections 63(1) and (2) do not apply to a person who remarries after the coming into force of this section.
@ref Act s 63.1(1) (src:2101)
GIVEN `the day the person remarries` IS A DATE
      `the day section 63.1 comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 63.1(1) — subsections 63(1) and (2) do not apply to the person` `the day the person remarries` `the day section 63.1 comes into force` MEANS
    -- "a person who remarries after the coming into force of this section"
    `the day the person remarries` GREATER THAN `the day section 63.1 comes into force`

§§ `Section 63(1) and (2) -- remarriage`

-- src:2076 | Where spouse remarried before survivor’s pension payable
-- src:2077 | 63 (1) Where a person whose spouse has died remarries at a time when no survivor’s pension is payable to him, no survivor’s pension is payable to that person during the period of his remarriage and if following the death of his spouse of that or any subsequent remarriage a survivor’s pension would be payable to him if he applied for such a pension, his deceased spouse for the purposes of this Act shall be deemed to be his spouse named in the application.
@ref Act s 63(1) (src:2077)
GIVEN `the person's spouse has died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person remarries at a time when no survivor's pension is payable to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is within the period of the remarriage on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the person remarries` IS A DATE
      `the day section 63.1 comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 63(1) — no survivor's pension is payable to the person on the day` `the person's spouse has died` `the person remarries at a time when no survivor's pension is payable to the person` `the person is within the period of the remarriage on the day` `the day the person remarries` `the day section 63.1 comes into force` MEANS
        `the person's spouse has died`
    AND `the person remarries at a time when no survivor's pension is payable to the person`
    AND `the person is within the period of the remarriage on the day`
    AND (NOT `s 63.1(1) — subsections 63(1) and (2) do not apply to the person` `the day the person remarries` `the day section 63.1 comes into force`)

-- src:2077 | 63 (1) Where a person whose spouse has died remarries at a time when no survivor’s pension is payable to him, no survivor’s pension is payable to that person during the period of his remarriage and if following the death of his spouse of that or any subsequent remarriage a survivor’s pension would be payable to him if he applied for such a pension, his deceased spouse for the purposes of this Act shall be deemed to be his spouse named in the application.
@ref Act s 63(1) (src:2077)
GIVEN `the person remarries at a time when no survivor's pension is payable to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a survivor's pension would be payable to the person, if the person applied, following the death of the spouse of that or any subsequent remarriage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the person remarries` IS A DATE
      `the day section 63.1 comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 63(1) — the first deceased spouse is deemed to be the spouse named in the application` `the person remarries at a time when no survivor's pension is payable to the person` `a survivor's pension would be payable to the person, if the person applied, following the death of the spouse of that or any subsequent remarriage` `the day the person remarries` `the day section 63.1 comes into force` MEANS
        `the person remarries at a time when no survivor's pension is payable to the person`
    AND `a survivor's pension would be payable to the person, if the person applied, following the death of the spouse of that or any subsequent remarriage`
    AND (NOT `s 63.1(1) — subsections 63(1) and (2) do not apply to the person` `the day the person remarries` `the day section 63.1 comes into force`)

-- src:2078 | Discontinuance of survivor’s pension
-- src:2079 | (2) Where a person to whom a survivor’s pension is being paid remarries, the survivor’s pension shall be discontinued commencing with the month following the month in which that person was married.
@ref Act s 63(2) (src:2079)
GIVEN `a survivor's pension is being paid to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the person is married` IS A DATE
      `the day section 63.1 comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 63(2) — the month from which the survivor's pension is discontinued` `a survivor's pension is being paid to the person` `the day the person is married` `the day section 63.1 comes into force` MEANS
    -- "discontinued commencing with the month following the month in which that person was married"; NOTHING where
    -- no pension is being paid, or where section 63.1(1) takes the remarriage out of subsection (2).
    IF   `a survivor's pension is being paid to the person`
     AND (NOT `s 63.1(1) — subsections 63(1) and (2) do not apply to the person` `the day the person is married` `the day section 63.1 comes into force`)
    THEN JUST (`the month following the month of a date` `the day the person is married`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 63(3) to (5) and (8) to (10) -- a discontinued pension`

-- src:2094 | Application of subsection (3)
-- src:2095 | (8) Subsection (3) applies only to a person who has made an application pursuant to that subsection that is pending on the coming into force of section 63.1.
@ref Act s 63(8) (src:2095)
GIVEN `the person has made an application under subsection (3) that is pending on the coming into force of section 63.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 63(8) — subsection (3) applies to the person` `the person has made an application under subsection (3) that is pending on the coming into force of section 63.1` MEANS
    `the person has made an application under subsection (3) that is pending on the coming into force of section 63.1`

-- src:2080 | Application for survivor’s pension
-- src:2081 | (3) Where the spouse of a person whose survivor’s pension has been discontinued under subsection (2) dies, that person may on application therefor be paid a survivor’s pension equal to the survivor’s pension that was discontinued under subsection (2) or the survivor’s pension that would have been payable by reason of the death of the spouse if no survivor’s pension had been previously payable to that person, whichever is the greater.
@ref Act s 63(3) (src:2081)
GIVEN `the person has made an application under subsection (3) that is pending on the coming into force of section 63.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's survivor's pension was discontinued under subsection (2) and the person's new spouse has died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the survivor's pension that was discontinued under subsection (2)` IS A NUMBER
      `the survivor's pension that would have been payable by reason of the death of the spouse if no survivor's pension had been previously payable to the person` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 63(3) — the survivor's pension payable to the person on application` `the person has made an application under subsection (3) that is pending on the coming into force of section 63.1` `the person's survivor's pension was discontinued under subsection (2) and the person's new spouse has died` `the survivor's pension that was discontinued under subsection (2)` `the survivor's pension that would have been payable by reason of the death of the spouse if no survivor's pension had been previously payable to the person` MEANS
    -- "equal to the survivor's pension that was discontinued ... or the survivor's pension that would have been payable
    -- ..., whichever is the greater"; NOTHING where subsection (3) does not apply (subsection (8)).
    IF   `s 63(8) — subsection (3) applies to the person` `the person has made an application under subsection (3) that is pending on the coming into force of section 63.1`
     AND `the person's survivor's pension was discontinued under subsection (2) and the person's new spouse has died`
    THEN JUST (max `the survivor's pension that was discontinued under subsection (2)` `the survivor's pension that would have been payable by reason of the death of the spouse if no survivor's pension had been previously payable to the person`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2096 | Application of subsection (4)
-- src:2097 | (9) Subsection (4) applies only to a person whose marriage is terminated as described in that subsection before the coming into force of section 63.1.
@ref Act s 63(9) (src:2097)
GIVEN `the day the marriage is terminated otherwise than by the death of the spouse` IS A DATE
      `the day section 63.1 comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 63(9) — subsection (4) applies to the person` `the day the marriage is terminated otherwise than by the death of the spouse` `the day section 63.1 comes into force` MEANS
    -- "a person whose marriage is terminated ... before the coming into force of section 63.1"
    `the day the marriage is terminated otherwise than by the death of the spouse` LESS THAN `the day section 63.1 comes into force`

-- src:2082 | Payment of pension to former spouse
-- src:2083 | (4) Where the marriage of a person whose survivor’s pension has been discontinued under subsection (2) is terminated otherwise than by the death of his spouse, the survivor’s pension previously payable to that person shall thereupon become payable to him.
@ref Act s 63(4) (src:2083)
GIVEN `the person's survivor's pension was discontinued under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the marriage is terminated otherwise than by the death of the spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the marriage is terminated otherwise than by the death of the spouse` IS A DATE
      `the day section 63.1 comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 63(4) — the survivor's pension previously payable becomes payable to the person again` `the person's survivor's pension was discontinued under subsection (2)` `the marriage is terminated otherwise than by the death of the spouse` `the day the marriage is terminated otherwise than by the death of the spouse` `the day section 63.1 comes into force` MEANS
        `the person's survivor's pension was discontinued under subsection (2)`
    AND `the marriage is terminated otherwise than by the death of the spouse`
    AND `s 63(9) — subsection (4) applies to the person` `the day the marriage is terminated otherwise than by the death of the spouse` `the day section 63.1 comes into force`

-- src:2098 | Subsection does not apply
-- src:2099 | (10) Subsection (5) does not apply in respect of a survivor’s pension that becomes payable pursuant to section 63.1.
@ref Act s 63(10) (src:2099)
GIVEN `the survivor's pension becomes payable pursuant to section 63.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 63(10) — subsection (5) applies to the survivor's pension` `the survivor's pension becomes payable pursuant to section 63.1` MEANS
    NOT `the survivor's pension becomes payable pursuant to section 63.1`

-- src:2084 | Calculation of basic amount of survivor’s pension
-- src:2085 | (5) Where a survivor’s pension payable to a person has been discontinued under subsection (2) and subsequently a survivor’s pension equal to the pension so discontinued becomes payable to that person or the pension so discontinued again becomes payable to him, the basic monthly amount of the pension thereupon payable to that person shall be calculated as though the pension discontinued under subsection (2) had not been discontinued.
@ref Act s 63(5) (src:2085)
GIVEN `a survivor's pension payable to the person has been discontinued under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a survivor's pension equal to the pension so discontinued becomes payable to the person, or the pension so discontinued again becomes payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the survivor's pension becomes payable pursuant to section 63.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 63(5) — the basic monthly amount is calculated as though the pension had not been discontinued` `a survivor's pension payable to the person has been discontinued under subsection (2)` `a survivor's pension equal to the pension so discontinued becomes payable to the person, or the pension so discontinued again becomes payable` `the survivor's pension becomes payable pursuant to section 63.1` MEANS
        `a survivor's pension payable to the person has been discontinued under subsection (2)`
    AND `a survivor's pension equal to the pension so discontinued becomes payable to the person, or the pension so discontinued again becomes payable`
    AND `s 63(10) — subsection (5) applies to the survivor's pension` `the survivor's pension becomes payable pursuant to section 63.1`

§§ `Section 63(6) -- only one survivor's pension`

-- src:2086 | Only one survivor’s pension payable
-- src:2087 | (6) Where, but for this subsection, more than one survivor’s pension would be payable concurrently to a person under this Act, or a survivor’s pension would be payable concurrently to a person under this Act and under a provincial pension plan, only one survivor’s pension shall be payable to that person, the amount of which shall be the greatest or greater of the survivor’s pensions that would, but for this subsection, be payable to that person.
@ref Act s 63(6) (src:2087)
GIVEN `the survivor's pensions that would, but for this subsection, be payable concurrently to the person under this Act and under a provincial pension plan` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 63(6) — the one survivor's pension payable to the person` `the survivor's pensions that would, but for this subsection, be payable concurrently to the person under this Act and under a provincial pension plan` MEANS
    -- "only one survivor's pension shall be payable to that person, the amount of which shall be the greatest or
    -- greater of the survivor's pensions that would, but for this subsection, be payable"; NOTHING if there are none.
    IF null `the survivor's pensions that would, but for this subsection, be payable concurrently to the person under this Act and under a provincial pension plan`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (maximum `the survivor's pensions that would, but for this subsection, be payable concurrently to the person under this Act and under a provincial pension plan`)

§§ `Section 63(7) and (7.1) -- death within a year of the marriage`

-- src:2090 | When subsection (7) does not apply
-- src:2091 | (7.1) Subsection (7) does not apply if the aggregate of the following periods is one year or more:
-- src:2092 | (a) the period during which the contributor and the survivor had cohabited during the marriage; and
-- src:2093 | (b) the period during which the contributor and the survivor had cohabited in a conjugal relationship immediately before the marriage.
@ref Act s 63(7.1) (src:2091-2093)
GIVEN `the number of days the contributor and the survivor cohabited during the marriage` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days the contributor and the survivor cohabited in a conjugal relationship immediately before the marriage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 63(7.1) — subsection (7) does not apply` `the number of days the contributor and the survivor cohabited during the marriage` `the number of days the contributor and the survivor cohabited in a conjugal relationship immediately before the marriage` MEANS
    -- "the aggregate of the following periods is one year or more": counted in days, a year being 365 days, since
    -- the periods are not tied to one start date (NOTES.md, fork register).
    (`the number of days the contributor and the survivor cohabited during the marriage` PLUS `the number of days the contributor and the survivor cohabited in a conjugal relationship immediately before the marriage`) AT LEAST 365

-- src:2088 | Death within 1 year of marriage
-- src:2089 | (7) Where a contributor dies within one year after his marriage, no survivor’s pension is payable to his survivor if the Minister is not satisfied that the contributor was at the time of his marriage in such a condition of health as to justify him in having an expectation of surviving for at least one year thereafter.
@ref Act s 63(7) (src:2089)
GIVEN `the day of the marriage` IS A DATE
      `the day the contributor died` IS A DATE
      `the Minister is satisfied that the contributor was at the time of the marriage in such a condition of health as to justify an expectation of surviving for at least one year thereafter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days the contributor and the survivor cohabited during the marriage` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days the contributor and the survivor cohabited in a conjugal relationship immediately before the marriage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 63(7) — no survivor's pension is payable because the contributor died within a year of the marriage` `the day of the marriage` `the day the contributor died` `the Minister is satisfied that the contributor was at the time of the marriage in such a condition of health as to justify an expectation of surviving for at least one year thereafter` `the number of days the contributor and the survivor cohabited during the marriage` `the number of days the contributor and the survivor cohabited in a conjugal relationship immediately before the marriage` MEANS
        `a date is within a time limit after a start date` `the day the contributor died` `the day of the marriage` (`a number of years` WITH `number of years` IS 1)
    AND (NOT `the Minister is satisfied that the contributor was at the time of the marriage in such a condition of health as to justify an expectation of surviving for at least one year thereafter`)
    AND (NOT `s 63(7.1) — subsection (7) does not apply` `the number of days the contributor and the survivor cohabited during the marriage` `the number of days the contributor and the survivor cohabited in a conjugal relationship immediately before the marriage`)

§ `Section 63.1 -- applying for a survivor's pension after section 63.1 comes into force`

-- src:2102 | Application for commencement or reinstatement of survivor’s pension
-- src:2103 | (2) Where, before the coming into force of subsection (1),
-- src:2104 | (a) a survivor’s pension that, but for the operation of subsection 63(1), would have become payable to a person did not become payable to the person, or
-- src:2105 | (b) the payment of a survivor’s pension to a person was discontinued under subsection 63(2),
-- src:2106 | and the person is not being paid a survivor’s pension at the time that this section comes into force, an application in writing to the Minister for the commencement or reinstatement, as the case may be, of the survivor’s pension may be made by the person or on behalf of the person by such other person as may be prescribed.
@ref Act s 63.1(2) (src:2103-2106)
GIVEN `a survivor's pension that, but for the operation of subsection 63(1), would have become payable to the person did not become payable, before section 63.1(1) came into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `payment of a survivor's pension to the person was discontinued under subsection 63(2) before section 63.1(1) came into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is not being paid a survivor's pension at the time that section 63.1 comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 63.1(2) — the person may apply in writing to the Minister for the commencement or reinstatement of the survivor's pension` `a survivor's pension that, but for the operation of subsection 63(1), would have become payable to the person did not become payable, before section 63.1(1) came into force` `payment of a survivor's pension to the person was discontinued under subsection 63(2) before section 63.1(1) came into force` `the person is not being paid a survivor's pension at the time that section 63.1 comes into force` MEANS
    -- The application may be made by the person, or on the person's behalf by a person prescribed (piece cr2).
        (   `a survivor's pension that, but for the operation of subsection 63(1), would have become payable to the person did not become payable, before section 63.1(1) came into force`
         OR `payment of a survivor's pension to the person was discontinued under subsection 63(2) before section 63.1(1) came into force`)
    AND `the person is not being paid a survivor's pension at the time that section 63.1 comes into force`

-- src:2107 | Commencement of survivor’s pension
-- src:2108 | (3) On approval by the Minister of an application referred to in subsection (2), a survivor’s pension is payable to the applicant for each month commencing with the later of
-- src:2109 | (a) the month in which this section comes into force, and
-- src:2110 | (b) the eleventh month preceding the month in which the application is received by the Minister.
@ref Act s 63.1(3) (src:2108-2110)
GIVEN `the day section 63.1 comes into force` IS A DATE
      `the day the Minister receives the application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 63.1(3) — the first month for which the survivor's pension is payable on approval` `the day section 63.1 comes into force` `the day the Minister receives the application` MEANS
    -- The later of (a) the month in which this section comes into force, and (b) the eleventh month preceding the
    -- month in which the application is received.
    `cp4 the later of two months` `the day section 63.1 comes into force` (`add months` (`the month of a date` `the day the Minister receives the application`) (0 MINUS 11))

-- src:2111 | Basic monthly amount of survivor’s pension
-- src:2112 | (4) Where a survivor’s pension becomes payable under this section to a person, the basic monthly amount of the pension shall be calculated in accordance with section 58 as though
-- src:2113 | (a) in the case of a person referred to in paragraph (2)(a), the survivor’s pension that would have become payable to the person but for the operation of subsection 63(1) became payable at the time that it would have become payable but for that subsection; and
-- src:2114 | (b) in the case of a person referred to in paragraph (2)(b), payment of the survivor’s pension to the person had not been discontinued under subsection 63(2).
@ref Act s 63.1(4) (src:2112-2114)
GIVEN `the person is a person referred to in paragraph (2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time at which the survivor's pension would have become payable but for the operation of subsection 63(1)` IS A DATE
      `the month with which payment of the survivor's pension discontinued under subsection 63(2) had commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 63.1(4) — the time from which the basic monthly amount is calculated in accordance with section 58` `the person is a person referred to in paragraph (2)(a)` `the time at which the survivor's pension would have become payable but for the operation of subsection 63(1)` `the month with which payment of the survivor's pension discontinued under subsection 63(2) had commenced` MEANS
    -- (a): "as though ... became payable at the time that it would have become payable but for that subsection";
    -- (b): "as though ... payment ... had not been discontinued": the pension runs from its original commencement.
    IF `the person is a person referred to in paragraph (2)(a)`
    THEN `the time at which the survivor's pension would have become payable but for the operation of subsection 63(1)`
    ELSE `the month with which payment of the survivor's pension discontinued under subsection 63(2) had commenced`
